    "body": "I personally prefer not using commas before and if there are only two \"simple\" things.\r\n\r\nWhat I don't understand here is that you still get a fresh view if the BYOB view cannot be written into due to its size. Wouldn't an error or request for a new view be more appropriate? If the idea is to avoid allocations presumably you would not want such allocations to nevertheless happen silently sometimes?",
